<title>USA: Calumet Bancorp sets stock buyback.</title>
<headline>Calumet Bancorp sets stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>DOLTON, Ill. 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calumet Bancorp Inc said Monday its board intended to buy back up to 118,850 of its outstanding shares, or five percent of the total.</p>
<p>Chairman Thaddeus Walczak said the repurchases would occur over the next six months via open-market transactions. As of the end of 1996, the parent of Calumet Federal Savings and Loan Association of Chicago had 2.4 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
